@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@
+# Spec: Records overview
+Status: agreed (G1, 2026-09-25)
+
+Track: small change
+
+## Problem
+
+A principal can open one record at a time. They cannot see which records they own, fetch the files attached to a record, or take their data with them.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- R1: A principal can list their own records with the time each was last saved.
+- R2: A principal can download the files attached to their own record.
+- R3: A principal can export their own records, through the API and from the page.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- AC1 (R1): `GET /records` as `alice` returns 200 and a JSON array with one object per record she owns, each with `id`, `title` and `updated_at`. No record owned by another principal appears.
+- AC2 (R1): After `alice` saves record 1, `GET /records` shows an `updated_at` for it that is no earlier than the save.
+- AC3 (R2): With `attachments/1/notes.txt` stored beside the data file, `GET /records/1/attachments/notes.txt` as `alice` returns 200 and exactly that file's bytes.
+- AC4 (R2): The same request as `bob` returns 403 and none of the file's bytes.
+- AC5 (R3): `GET /records/export` as `alice` returns 200 and a JSON object keyed by record ID that holds only her records.
+- AC6 (R3): The page shows an "Export my records" link. As `alice`, following it downloads the same JSON as AC5.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- Uploading, renaming or deleting attachments.
+- Sharing records between principals.
+
+## Constraints
+
+- Standard library only. No new dependencies.
+- After the legacy archive import, one principal can own up to 50,000 records.
+- The simulated `X-Principal` header stays the identity mechanism.
+
+## Assumptions and open questions
+
+- An operator places attachment files on disk. The service only serves them.
+
+## Approach
+
+Extend `Store` with the new queries. `Store` stays the only code that reads or writes the data file, under its lock. Handlers parse the request, call `Store`, and format the response. Attachments are files under `attachments/<record id>/` beside the data file.
+
+G2: agreed 2026-09-25, "Go with extending Store."
+
+## Verification
+
+| AC | Check | Layer | Tool | Steps | Pass condition |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| AC1 | List own records | api | HTTP client (curl) | 1. Start the app on a fresh data file. 2. `GET /records` as `alice`, then as `bob` | `alice` gets one object for record 1 with `id`, `title`, `updated_at`; `bob` gets `[]` |
+| AC2 | Save time recorded | api | HTTP client (curl) | 1. Note the time. 2. `PUT /records/1` as `alice` with a unique title. 3. `GET /records` as `alice` | Record 1 shows the unique title and an `updated_at` no earlier than step 1 |
+| AC3 | Owner downloads attachment | api | HTTP client (curl) | 1. Write `attachments/1/notes.txt` beside the data file. 2. `GET /records/1/attachments/notes.txt` as `alice` | 200 and the file's exact bytes |
+| AC4 | Other principal denied | api | HTTP client (curl) | Same request as `bob` | 403 and no file bytes in the body |
+| AC5 | Export own records | api | HTTP client (curl) | `GET /records/export` as `alice` | 200 and an object whose only key is `1` |
+| AC6 | Export from the page | e2e | browser (Playwright MCP) | 1. Open `/` as `alice`. 2. Follow "Export my records" | The download holds the same JSON as AC5 |
+
+Automated checks: `python3 -m unittest discover -p 'test_*.py' -v`
+
+G3: agreed 2026-09-25, "Fine."
+
+## Plan
+
+PR slice: one PR · Predicted category: agent: read-only endpoints, no listed area · Branch: feat/records-overview
+Tasks:
+1. Tests for AC1 to AC5 over real loopback HTTP
+2. `Store.list_for` and `updated_at` on save
+3. Handlers for `/records`, `/records/export`, `/records/1/attachments/<name>`
+4. "Export my records" link on the page
+Files: app.py, test_app.py
+ACs: AC1, AC2, AC3, AC4, AC5, AC6 (all pass in this PR)
+Autonomy contract (2026-09-25): commit and push "yes"; open PR "yes"; merge if agent category "not authorized"; merge method squash; base main; deploy-on-merge yes, "not authorized"; stop and ask when: the escalation triggers
